# Implementation Plan - HOTFIX-009 — Overlay Visibility / Opacity Control

Implement an "Overlay Visibility" control panel at the bottom-center area of the main BatmanOverlay UI (below content area and above status bar) allowing users to adjust window transparency from 0% (fully visible) to 100% (fully transparent).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The transparency percentage value $T$ (0–100) maps strictly to Qt window opacity $O$ (0.0–1.0) via:
> $$O = 1.0 - (T / 100.0)$$
> - $T=0\%$   $\rightarrow O=1.0$ (Fully Opaque / Visible)
> - $T=25\%$  $\rightarrow O=0.75$
> - $T=50\%$  $\rightarrow O=0.50$
> - $T=75\%$  $\rightarrow O=0.25$
> - $T=100\%$ $\rightarrow O=0.0$ (Fully Transparent / Invisible)
>
> Settings persistence is integrated into the existing `ConfigManager` via `appearance.overlay_transparency`.

## Proposed Changes

### UI & Window Integration

#### [NEW] [overlay_visibility_panel.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/overlay_visibility_panel.py)
- Create `OverlayVisibilityPanel` widget (inherits `QWidget`).
- Layout hierarchy:
  - Header: Title `"Overlay Visibility"`, Subtitle `"Adjust the transparency of the overlay"`, Value Label `"0%"`, Reset Button (`"Reset"`).
  - Slider row: Left Endpoint `"0% (Fully Visible)"`, `QSlider` (0 to 100, default 0, `StrongFocus` for keyboard accessibility), Right Endpoint `"100% (Fully Transparent)"`.
- Connect slider `valueChanged` signal to update numeric label and emit `transparency_changed(int)`.
- Connect reset button to set slider value back to `0`.

#### [MODIFY] [__init__.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/__init__.py)
- Export `OverlayVisibilityPanel`.

#### [MODIFY] [main_window.py](file:///c:/github/batmanoverlay.com/src/ui/main_window.py)
- Instantiate `OverlayVisibilityPanel` in `MainWindow._setup_ui()` and insert it into `root_layout` below `_content_widget` and above `status_bar`.
- Connect `overlay_visibility_panel.transparency_changed` to `_on_transparency_changed(transparency: int)`:
  - Computes $O = 1.0 - (transparency / 100.0)$.
  - Calls `setWindowOpacity(O)`.
  - Saves setting `appearance.overlay_transparency` via `ConfigManager`.
  - Triggers debounced geometry save timer.
- On geometry/settings restore, sync `OverlayVisibilityPanel` transparency slider value and window opacity.
- Adjust `set_window_opacity` clamping from `[0.1, 1.0]` to `[0.0, 1.0]` to allow 100% transparency ($O=0.0$).

